The README now states the key limitation plainly: this is a paper-licensed factor-trapdoor task, not native curve arithmetic, and the G9 hint result shows it measures computation more than insight. I also found one escalation-boundary issue—the existing cap stopped at 1024-bit factors even though one 1088-bit rung may still fit—so I’m moving the boundary to the last measured writable rung before final validation.
